@title Electric Reliability, January to September 2026
@subtitle Data summary for the state regulator and the board
@author Sven Lindqvist, Reliability Engineer
@date 2026-09-30

# Reliability at a glance

kpi Avg outage per customer | 99.6 min | target 105 min | good
kpi Customers served | 412,000 | 5 districts | neutral
kpi Outage events | 177 | Jan to Sep | neutral

The system as a whole meets the regulator's target of 105 minutes. Three districts do not: Hills (176), Plains (131) and Coastal (112). Hills is the worst by a wide margin.

# By district

Minutes below are the average outage time per customer, with the 105-minute target shown as a dashed line.

data districts = district,customers,events,minutes,target; Hills,61000,37,176,105; Plains,24000,19,131,105; Coastal,98000,41,112,105; Valley,142000,58,84,105; Metro,87000,22,49,105

chart hbar districts x=district y=minutes target="105 target" unit=" min" labels title="Average outage minutes per customer"

chart hbar districts x=district y=customers sort title="Customers by district"

table districts cols=district,customers,events,minutes,target bar=minutes target=target sort=-minutes title="Districts, worst first"

!! Hills, Plains and Coastal are above the 105-minute target. Hills at 176 minutes is 68% over it.

! Metro's low figure of 49 minutes reflects its underground cables.

# Causes

data causes = cause,share; Storms,46; Equipment failure,27; Vegetation,15; Other,12

chart hbar causes x=cause y=share unit=% labels title="Share of outage minutes by cause"

Storms and equipment failure account for 73% of outage minutes. Vegetation, at 15%, is the cause the Hills program targets.

# Next steps

step Start the Hills tree-trimming program | 2026-11-02

The program was approved with a budget of $1.8M and covers 210 line miles.
